From 5275e3c9ab3ddc28d6c78a20e1056d6ab33cdd2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dev <dev@example.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 08:33:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] B2: redaction/denylist layer, two-form
 (eo/redaction_guard.py)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New backend/eo/redaction_guard.py: the hard-coded enforcement half
  of the denylist. is_readable(path) -> bool checks an explicit
  ALLOWED_ROOTS allowlist (backend/eo, backend/agents, backend/api,
  backend/tests, docs, cli, frontend/app, DEFERRED.md, README.md) with
  os.path.commonpath-based containment (so `..` traversal can't escape
  a nominally-allowed root), then a SECRET_NAME_PATTERNS filename check
  (.env*, *secret*, *credential*, *api_key*, id_rsa/id_ed25519/.pem/
  .pfx/.p12) even for paths inside an allowed root. No import of
  eo.capability_entries or eo.capabilities anywhere in this file --
  the whole point is that the answer holds with zero trust in that
  (model-writable) data layer. Denies rather than raises, so a
  rejection doesn't leak why.
- backend/eo/capability_entries.py: write_capability_entry() now takes
  an optional user_id and, when entry_type="redaction", logs the write
  via eo/audit_log.py::write_audit() (falls back to a
  "system:capability_entries" actor if no user_id is given, same
  posture chat_workspace.py's _AUTO_PROMOTE_ACTOR takes). Ordinary
  entry_type="capability" writes are not audited -- not a security
  boundary, would just be noise next to the redaction changes that
  matter.
- DEFERRED.md: one new entry -- redaction_guard.py's ALLOWED_ROOTS/
  SECRET_NAME_PATTERNS are a code change, not a config change, unlike
  the documentation-half redaction entries; revisit alongside the
  already-deferred drift-check mechanism, not before.
- Tests: backend/tests/unit/test_eo_redaction_guard.py (allowed-root
  boundary incl. traversal, secret-pattern denial incl. an
  incidental-substring false-positive check, degenerate input, and the
  actual acceptance property -- a deliberately permissive/malicious
  redaction entry written to capability_entries.py does not change
  is_readable()'s answer); extends test_eo_capability_entries.py with
  redaction-write-logs-audit / capability-write-does-not / missing-
  user_id-falls-back-to-system-actor / repeat-write-marks-created-false.
- Full backend unit suite re-run after this patch: 3433 passed, 7
  skipped, 2 xfailed, 0 failed (pre-existing skips/xfails, unrelated to
  this change).

Ref: MiniMe-CLI-Internal-Architecture-Plan.md §3.2 (why the denylist needs two forms)
Ref: MiniMe-Patch-Series-B-Plan.md, Patch B2
Depends on: Patch B1 (eo/capability_entries.py's entry_type mechanism must exist)
